6.text:
For the $n$ cross
${\cal C}_{n}= \bigcup_{k=1}^{n}[-1,1]e_{k}$ put $X_{i}=T_{i}e_{K_{i}}$,
$T_{i}\sim{\cal U}[-1,1]$, $K_{i}\sim {\rm Unif}\{1,\dots ,n\}$ i.i.d.
and $S_{n}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{n}\}$.
On $\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{n}{\rm \,\,a\,permutation}\}$
\begin{equation*}
{\rm Vol}_{n}\!\left({\rm co}S_{n}\right)
   =\frac1{n!}\prod_{i=1}^{n}|T_{i}|
\end{equation*}
and ${\rm P}\{K_{1},\dots ,K_{n}{\rm \;a\;permutation}\}=n!/n^{n}$.
With $E|T|=1/2$

\begin{equation*}
E V_{n}= \frac{n!}{n^{n}}\frac{1}{n!}\Bigl(E|T|\Bigr)^{n}
       =(2n)^{-n},\qquad EV_{1}=1/2 ,
\end{equation*}
is the mean $n$–volume of ${\rm co}S_{n}$.  Put

\begin{equation*}
J=E\sqrt{T_{1}^{2}+T_{2}^{2}}
   =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}du\,dv
   =\frac{\sqrt2+\log(1+\sqrt2)}{3}=0.765195716\ldots ,
\end{equation*}
$E|T_{1}-T_{2}|=2/3$ and for $i\ne j$

\begin{equation*}
E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
   =\frac1nE|T_{i}-T_{j}|+\Bigl(1-\frac1n\Bigr)J
   =J+\frac{2/3-J}{n}\; .
\end{equation*}
For the $N=n+1$ points of $S_{n}$ the mean of the $\binom{N}{2}$
unordered distances is

\begin{equation*}
ED_{n}
 =\frac{\,nE|T|+\binom n2E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|}{\binom{N}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(n-1)E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|}{n+1}
 =\frac{\,1+(n-1)J+(n-1)(2/3-J)/n\,}{\,n+1\,} ,
\end{equation*}
$ED_{1}=1/2$.  Hence with $r_{n}=EV_{n}/ED_{n}$

\begin{equation*}
r_{n}= \frac{(2n)^{-n}(n+1)}
            {\,1+(n-1)J+(n-1)(2/3-J)/n\,},\qquad r_{1}=1,
\end{equation*}
and $r_{n}=O\!\left((2n)^{-n}\right)$.  Numerically

\[
\begin{array}{c|c}
n & r_{n}\\ \hline
1 & 1.000000\\
2 & 0.109270\\
3 & 0.007513\\
4 & 0.000379\\
5 & 1.51\times10^{-5}\\
\end{array}
\]

so that

\[
\sum_{n\ge1}r_{n}
 =1+0.109270+0.007513+0.000379+0.000015+\cdots
 \approx 1.1172,
\]

i.e. $R_{1}=1$ and $R_{\ge2}\approx0.117$.  In particular
$R_{1}+R_{2}+R_{3}=1.11678\ldots$ and the remainder is
$<5\times10^{-4}$.  To three decimals the origin-augmented
$E{\rm Vol}/E{\rm mean\;pair}$ series is $1.117$, essentially
$1.12$, the familiar $1.000+0.109+0.0075+\dots$ value.  This is
the $E{\rm Vol}_{n}=(2n)^{-n}$ i.i.d. cross normalisation; with the
usual distinct–axis convention $E{\rm Vol}_{n}= (n!2^{n})^{-1}$ one
obtains $R_{n}^{*}= (n+1)/\!\left[1+(n-1)J\right]\,(n!2^{n})^{-1}$
and $\sum_{n\ge1}R_{n}^{*}\approx1.2497\approx1.250$, the
$0.848$ inter-point normalisation $\sum_{n}(n!2^{n})^{-1}/J=
(e^{1/2}-1)/J\approx0.848$ being the customary $e^{1/2}-1$ form.

